        ":question/problem": "Find ${f}^{″}(x)$ for $f(x)={x}^{6}+{x}^{5}.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({x}^{6}+{x}^{5})}^{′} \\\\  & =6\\cdot {x}^{5}+5\\cdot {x}^{4} \\\\  & =6{x}^{5}+5{x}^{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & ={(6{x}^{5}+5{x}^{4})}^{′} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 6{x}^{4}+4\\cdot 5{x}^{3} \\\\  & =30{x}^{4}+20{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
